{"archetypes":[{"name":"bash-parity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Large Python port claims exact bash parity for finalize, merge, cleanup, postbump, and teardown flows.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether the Python changes preserve the observable behavior of the referenced bash implementations, especially status tokens, branch transitions, retry ordering, and cleanup side effects. Compare the intended control-flow ordering against the modified Python call graph and the new parity tests. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"runlog-recovery","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Manifest recovery and fail-closed run-log behavior now span run_logs, ship, merge, and finalize teardown paths.","prompt_body":"Review the manifest recovery, final-report rendering, log flush, and commit gating paths across run-log producers and consumers. Look for paths that still write done manifests, reports, commits, or sentinels after recovery failure, or that incorrectly turn warning-only ship paths into terminal failures. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ci-rebase-state","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"CI_FIX_REBASE_PENDING introduces persisted state that affects push versus force-push behavior across restarts.","prompt_body":"Examine how CI_FIX_REBASE_PENDING is hydrated, serialized, updated, and cleared through RunContext, CI monitor results, ship-state persistence, and retry loops. Pay special attention to whether force-push is limited to the intended rebase cases and whether pending push retries survive process restarts without duplicating or losing state. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"timing-ledger","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds cross-workflow timing ledger rows for design plan review and implement code review rounds.","prompt_body":"Inspect the new timing-ledger integrations in design and review-and-fix scripts for consistent schema, idempotency, ordering, and stale-environment isolation. Check terminal, deferred, retry, and early-exit paths to ensure round rows are emitted exactly once with accurate start, end, duration, and count fields. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-portability","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"Many new shell helpers and harnesses must remain portable under the repository bash and quiet-output conventions.","prompt_body":"Review modified shell scripts for Bash 3.2 compatibility, robust quoting, safe temp-file handling, trap cleanup, quiet-by-default output, and interaction with sourced helper libraries. Focus on subtle portability issues in awk, grep, arrays, local variables, symlink checks, and environment propagation. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
